+# A01 / E02 — accessible controls and explicit microphone recovery
+
+Source implementation, 2026-10-30. No Apple build, Swift test, microphone, model, audible VoiceOver or physical-device execution was performed for this patch. Tracker IDs refer to `research/tracker-reconciliation-20261028/TRACKER.json`, not the older differently numbered TASKS families. A01/E02 remain open pending native/device acceptance.
+
+## Concrete changes
+
+1. **Terminal microphone recovery is explicit.** The existing `VoiceCaptureRecoveryPolicy` retains a restart hold after terminal failure, exhausted three-attempt recovery, private-route loss or a system interruption ending without resume permission. Cancel, foreground, language change, media reset and automatic answer windows cannot erase the hold. Only the existing explicit `NavigationModel.startConversation` route supplies `explicitlyRequested: true`; permission, offline-recognition, session-generation, OS-interruption and background checks remain in place. Ordinary recoverable interruption/retry behavior stays bounded. The hold is ephemeral, not a saved permission or speaker-identity claim.
+2. **Accessible recovery and quiet/resume controls.** An active session whose capture is held now exposes Reconnect microphone instead of only Mute. Mute and End remain available. Conversation controls gain a reachable descriptions toggle with a localized accessibility value; it uses the existing stop/resume functions and neither starts microphone/camera nor restores a cancelled task. The unused older `actions` view was not evidence of actual control reachability.
+3. **Ask layout candidate.** The finite Ask screen uses the already used Camera `ScrollView`/eager `VStack` layout and minimum-height button style, with semantic section headers, multiline text, native inline selection, labelled input fields and the exact disabled-camera explanation. There is no size cap, truncation, hidden warning or accessibility-audit exemption. Earlier audit callbacks do **not** establish lazy Form sizing as the cause. Native audit and actual VoiceOver behavior are still required to validate this candidate.
+4. **Newly triggered accessibility CI storage is off by default.** Its two existing artifact uploads now require the same explicit source opt-in as the other relevant lanes. Retention remains three days if separately enabled; nothing is deleted. Existing layout/audit commands and failure handling remain unchanged. The shared bounded receipt emitter emits only job/step outcomes for this lane, into normal logs/summary, and reads no image or arbitrary JSON. Build/test output remains in normal job logs. No runner, service, dependency, cache or paid storage assumption was added.
+
+## Retained evidence, not overwritten
+
+- Actual `08ebe14` UI: Ask audit failed with two Dynamic Type findings (one names `local-answer-unavailable-reason`, the other has no identified element). Its practice cancellation witness passed: explicit End, elapsed upper bound **4.566708208333694 s < 90 s**.
+- Actual `e418290`: same audit failure family; explicit practice End upper bound **8.100812583333436 s < 90 s**. These are source-bound simulator results, not this patch's results or physical microphone/VoiceOver proof.
+- Both existing 90-second before/after End guards and the production 120-second expiry are byte-preserved. The full camera/Ask audit body is byte-preserved, including its sole pre-existing inactive-return-control contrast exemption. No failed test was removed or counted as passing.
+- Earlier model-generation failures (`available` with `generationFailed`/missing replies), native timing failures, collision/contact failures and 799 focused-collector/QoS failures remain unresolved by this batch. This patch does not claim an on-device model or complete everyday-goal result.
+
+## Tests and verification
+
+Authored but **not executed natively**: five additional Core lifecycle methods (12 retained + 5 = 17), three controller/source-retention methods (25 retained + 3 = 28 in the existing hosted file), two UI control/reachability methods (17 retained + 2 = 19 in LaunchTests). The privacy-restart test retains its original assertions and now also rejects automatic begin before explicit restart. The completion test preserves exact parent source ID/request/time and user-reported completion across pause/restore; it does not infer possession, arrival or a fresh movement action.
+
+Executed locally: `python3 tools/test/accessibility-voice-continuity.test.py` — two source-only methods cover 28 contracts plus 11 rejected mutations. `python3 tools/ci/test_emit_ci_log_receipts.py` — 26 stdlib tests (23 retained + 3 accessibility controls) pass. These are source/synthetic parser checks, not Swift execution. The tiny isolated test overlay contains only source and workflow inputs.
+
+## Integration / remaining work
+
+The isolated before snapshot includes the locally applied, separately reviewed mapped-destination source on published 799; only one line changes in NavigationModel. Apply the patch against exact before hashes, not a whole-file copy over newer source. Add the changed/new files to current manifests and a new reversible integrated provenance layer before publication; do not rewrite historical hashes. Full trigger audit must be rerun after those provenance paths are added.
+
+No new project membership is required: native tests append to existing target members and Core discovery includes its existing file. Expected current patch push triggers: native Apple (three jobs), current body profile, and focused accessibility diagnostic. All are public/fork guarded standard `xcode-27`; uploads default off. The accessibility observer's `BLIND_CI_JOB` line preserves layout failure even where the original layout step has `continue-on-error: true`; later `Retain diagnostic failure status` still exits 1. Screenshots remain runner-local, not uploaded.
+
+Next execution is root's reviewed source publication, not this preparation. Read exact-commit native results for all original tests plus new cases, both 90s guards, unsuppressed Dynamic Type audit, Reconnect and quiet/resume reachability. Actual permission denial, phone-call interruption, media reset, headset removal, mute/end, foreground/background and microphone/VoiceOver coordination require device verification. Use the user's supervised acceptance sequence; no physical guidance or independent child use is approved.
+
+Platform references (reuse, not new engines): [Apple inline Picker](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/SwiftUI/InlinePickerStyle), [scrollable stacks](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/creating-performant-scrollable-stacks), [Dynamic Type](https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2024/10074/). Existing AVFoundation/Speech capture and existing code-owned goal/source policies are retained.
